  "articleBody": "Picking out new kitchen countertops can feel like a big decision, right? There are so many options, and you want to make sure you're getting something that looks great and truly works for your home. When you’re making your choice, think about how much wear and tear your kitchen gets. Are you a gourmet chef, or do you mostly use it for quick meals? This helps narrow down materials based on durability and how much maintenance they’ll need. Some materials require regular sealing, while others are pretty much set-it-and-forget-it. You'll also want to consider things like heat and stain resistance – nobody wants a permanent ring from a hot pan or a spilled glass of wine! Of course, your budget is a big factor, and there are fantastic options at every price point. Finally, always make sure your installer is licensed and insured, with good experience, especially if you're looking at natural stone or anything with complex cuts. We’re here to help guide you through all these choices to find the perfect fit for your Denver-area home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
